V8: "[builtins] Track Promise.any reject closure state in the errors array"
(crbug 578688670; no CVE listed yet): a Promise.any reject element closure
marked itself called by replacing its own context, which Maglev and TurboFan
constant-fold, so optimized code could call it repeatedly, completing the
AggregateError with PromiseHole entries still in its errors array: memory
corruption reachable from page JavaScript. V8 main commit
85adfcb327156366bd8d3412a349247995ab4c65, merged on 2026-10-31 to 15.7
(45a2a987887d879123039468a362bef9cf506167, for 157; after the
157.0.8103.34 tag) and proposed for 15.6. This is the 15.7 merge, at v8/,
without its test. Drop it once a 157 tag's V8 has it.

